      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Level, momentum, one-off, and policy-mechanism effects: level starts from June's 541.96 thousand. Momentum is slightly negative, with May and June declines of 0.75 and 1.73 thousand. One-off risk is that summer employment strength in July may reduce new EI inflow before the August employment decline shows up. Policy-mechanism effect is limited because the resolver is an administrative beneficiary stock; eligibility and benefit exhaustion mean LFS unemployment moves do not map one-for-one into EI beneficiaries."
      },
